# {{DIST}}

A PULSE inbound connector scaffolded from `templates/connector/` by
`uv run python scripts/connector_new.py --name {{DIST}} --direction inbound`.

Inbound means this connector *reads*: it pages a source system through the kit's inbound read
contract (`RowSource`, `CursorStore`), validates each page against a pinned column contract, and
declares what validated. The outbound variant — consume the bus, derive, declare — is what
`--direction outbound` (the default) renders.

## What is here

| Path | What to do with it |
| --- | --- |
| `src/{{NAME}}/config.py` | Add the variables this connector reads. `from_env` already collects every problem into one error. |
| `src/{{NAME}}/service.py` | Pin `CONTRACT_COLUMNS` and `SourceRow`, replace `build_row_source` with the real adapter, then `handle_page` with what this connector declares. |
| `src/{{NAME}}/receipts.py` | Add this connector's own counts alongside the kit's three and this variant's `read` / `invalid`. |
| `tests/conftest.py` | Do not weaken it. Sockets are blocked for every run that collects this package. |
| `tests/test_service.py` | The reader's contract: validation, the durable cursor, resume. Extend it as the reader grows. |
| `tests/test_receipts.py` | The receipt-line golden. Extend it as `Receipt` grows. |

